openbindings.md
ob works with OpenBindings interface documents (OBIs): create and edit
them, check them, compare them with shared contracts, and use them to call
the services they describe.

PREVIEW: this build shows the proposed command surface. Commands answer from
a built-in sample document (a Task Manager API); nothing is read, written,
or called.

Usage:
  ob [flags]
  ob [command]

Examples:
  ob init tasks.obi.json --name "Task Manager"
  ob operation add tasks.obi.json createTask --input-schema '{"type":"object"}'
  ob source add tasks.obi.json httpApi --kind example.openapi@1 --content '{"location":"https://api.example.com/openapi.json"}'
  ob binding add tasks.obi.json createTask.http --operation createTask --source httpApi --content '{"target":"#/paths/~1tasks/post"}'
  ob validate tasks.obi.json
  ob invoke tasks.obi.json createTask --input '{"title":"Write the docs"}'

Documents
  init        Create a new OBI
  show        Show a document
  validate    Check a document, a value, or examples
  diff        Compare two documents
  compat      Check a document against a shared contract
  fmt         Format documents
  patch       Apply a JSON Patch
  merge       Bring operations in from another document

Parts of a document
  operation   Add, change, and remove operations
  source      Add, change, and remove sources, and read their artifacts
  binding     Add, change, and remove bindings
  dependency  Add, change, and remove dependencies
  schema      Add, change, and remove reusable schemas

Sources
  synthesize  Create a document from an artifact
  status      Show how a document has drifted from its sources

Using a service
  fetch       Download a service's OBI
  invoke      Call an operation
  context     Store credentials and settings for calls
  codegen     Generate a typed client

Serving
  start       Run ob as a local service
  mcp         Serve a document's operations as MCP tools

Kinds and delegates
  kind        See which kinds this ob can handle
  delegate    Let other tools handle work for ob

Additional Commands:
  help        Help about any command

Flags:
      --agent-primer   print the OpenBindings primer for AI agents and exit
  -h, --help           help for ob
      --openbindings   print ob's own OBI and exit
      --usage-spec     print ob's usage spec (usage.kdl) and exit
  -v, --version        version for ob

Use "ob [command] --help" for more information about a command.

