1:# OpenBindings Specification (v0.2.0)
3:## Abstract
5:OpenBindings is a portable interface description format; its documents are OBIs (OpenBindings interface documents). An OBI declares each operation once, as a protocol-independent contract with optional per-value input and output schemas, then relates it to concrete realizations through bindings and to named consumption points through dependencies. The contract lives at the operation layer; protocols live at the binding layer.
