39:The kinds in this document's examples (`example.openapi@1`, `example.mcp@1`, `example.grpc@1`, `my-cli.usage@1`) and the shapes of their `content`, such as `{ "location": … }` on a source and `{ "target": … }` on a binding, are illustrative; only a kind gives `content` meaning ([§6](#6-kinds)).
41:New readers may prefer the [§4. Overview](#4-overview-informative) walkthrough. From [§2. Core invariants](#2-core-invariants) on, the text is normative except where marked informative; conformance is judged by the numbered rules of [§10](#10-conformance).
